# Large ratios: no upper rejection (the plan's quirk). ratio_sq beyond f(200),
# 10.036952025966171, moves c_lo at every step and the return saturates at the upper
# bound 200, which binds (c_hi never moves); just below f(200) it does not quite. Vvir 1
# unless stated.
# Reachability: constructed routine-domain probe.
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine concentration_from_vmax_vvir
i32 call.ncase 6
# case[0]: ratio_sq just below f(200)
f64 case[0].Vmax 0x4009584c19d6890a  # 3.168113901004408
f64 case[0].Vvir 0x3ff0000000000000  # 1.0
# case[1]: ratio_sq at sqrt(f(200)) squared
f64 case[1].Vmax 0x4009584ca00e4610  # 3.168114901004408
f64 case[1].Vvir 0x3ff0000000000000  # 1.0
# case[2]: ratio_sq 2.25 f(200)
f64 case[2].Vmax 0x40130239780ab48c  # 4.752172351506612
f64 case[2].Vvir 0x3ff0000000000000  # 1.0
# case[3]: Vmax / Vvir = 10: ratio_sq 100
f64 case[3].Vmax 0x409f400000000000  # 2000.0
f64 case[3].Vvir 0x4069000000000000  # 200.0
# case[4]: ratio_sq 1e300
f64 case[4].Vmax 0x5f138d352e5096af  # 1e+150
f64 case[4].Vvir 0x3ff0000000000000  # 1.0
# case[5]: Vmax / Vvir overflows to +inf
f64 case[5].Vmax 0x6974e718d7d7625a  # 1e+200
f64 case[5].Vvir 0x16687e92154ef7ac  # 1e-200
